What comes from the original (GPL v2), converted by tools/convert.mjs from tuxracer-0.61.tar.gz and
tuxracer-data_0.61.orig.tar.gz (scripts/fetch-tuxracer.sh fetches them, sha256-pinned):
  assets/courses/*         the 13 courses: the height, terrain and object rasters, names, par times
                           (the contributed courses name their authors in each course's course.tcl)
  assets/model/tux.json    the Tux model (tux.tcl) and the walk-in keyframes (tux_walk.tcl)
  assets/music/*.it        the Impulse Tracker music by Joseph Toscano
  assets/sounds/*.wav      the sound effects
  assets/original/*        the original textures (terrain tiles, sky cubes, items, HUD art)
The physics constants, the camera and the rules are ported from the original source (phys_sim.c,
view.c, game_logic_util.c).

Made for this reimplementation (GPL-2.0-or-later with the game):
  src/*, shaders/*.mjs     the game, its Box3D sliding and its shader parts
  tools/make-sky.mjs       the mountain ring (from the original sky cubes and a photograph of Mount
                           Rainier taken from a plane by Luis Montes), the cloud deck, the snow detail texture
  tools/make-sprig.mjs, tools/make-luts.mjs   the branch sprig texture and the colour grades
  src/tree_mesh.c, src/item_mesh.c, src/tux_skin.c   the generated conifers, herring, gates and the skinned Tux
  assets/textures/needles*, bark*, assets/model/trees.bin   needle and bark textures and the birch mesh from
                           Sky Fighter (games/skyfighter in this repository, tools/extract-trees.mjs)

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, licence files beside them in assets/fonts).

Engine: cartwheel-engine (MIT), three.c (MIT), Box2D and Box3D (MIT), as shipped with this
repository's build. The GPL permits linking them.
